    "caption": "The four steps behind one HTTPS request: DNS turns the name into an address, then TCP, TLS and HTTP happen against the load balancer, which forwards plain HTTP to whichever backends pass its health checks.",
    "alt": "A client asks a DNS resolver for the address of api.example.com, then opens TCP on port 443 and a TLS session to the load balancer, and sends the HTTP request. The load balancer forwards HTTP on port 8000 to two healthy application instances and skips a third that failed its health check. The instances query a database on port 5432.",
